    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "The GEO Community is an open, experiment-driven community for learning AI SEO, Answer Engine Optimization (AEO), and Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) — the work of improving how brands get cited in ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Gemini, and Copilot.",
      "Our goal: help the industry move from \"opinions about AI visibility\" to a practical, measurement-first framework for optimizing content that gets cited by LLMs.",
      "Traditional SEO optimized for rank → click → conversion. Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) optimizes for how brands show up in AI answers — where decisions happen before the click or without a click at all. This includes getting cited in ChatGPT answers, appearing in Perplexity sources, showing up in Google AI Overviews citations, and being recommended by Copilot.",
      "AI SEO vs AEO vs GEO explained: GEO vs SEO: How the User Funnel Has Changed • AEO vs GEO (Microsoft's framing)",
      "We're the best resource to learn AI SEO, AEO, and GEO — combining research breakdowns (including the GEO Princeton paper summary), implementation guides (robots.txt for AI bots, llms.txt guide, server-side rendering for AI crawlers), GEO experiments across ChatGPT, Perplexity, and Gemini, and measurement tools (how to track AI traffic in GA4, LLM citation tracking).",
      "This is explicitly different from \"tips for writing for AI\" — we teach you how to optimize for AI answers as a discipline where you become better evidence inside systems you can't fully observe.",
      "AI search optimization learning path: Start Here →",
      "1) Generative engines changed the funnel: visibility in answers → trust → decision → (maybe) click. Classic SEO metrics don't fully represent influence anymore.",
      "2) Engines don't behave the same: One-size-fits-all playbooks fail because each engine lives in a different information ecosystem.",
      "3) AI visibility → revenue: When AI surfaces become the checkout (Shopify + ChatGPT's 4% fee), optimization stops being \"nice to have.\" Read more →"
    ],
