    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "A story-style timeline of the algorithm updates that reshaped SEO — from PageRank to AI Overviews — and what each era means for Generative Engine Optimization.",
      "Google's early years were defined by a single insight: links are votes. PageRank turned the web's hyperlink structure into a democratic ranking system. For nearly a decade, SEO was fundamentally a link-building game — the sites with the most (and highest-quality) links won. Content quality was secondary.",
      "As Google added more answer features to the SERP, the space available for traditional organic results shrank — making source authority and citability more important than ever.",
      "The game changed. Google declared war on content farms and link spam, elevating the importance of creating genuinely useful content for users, not just search engines. Two updates — Panda and Penguin — reshaped the entire industry and established content quality and link quality as first-class ranking signals.",
      "This era marked a pivotal shift from matching keywords to understanding the meaning behind them. With Hummingbird, Google began to grasp conversational search, while updates like Pigeon and Mobilegeddon emphasized local context and mobile usability. RankBrain introduced machine learning to query interpretation.",
      "Each era didn't replace the previous one — it built on top of it. Links still matter. Content quality still matters. But each era added a new layer of sophistication.",
      "Machine learning took center stage. RankBrain helped Google interpret ambiguous queries, while BERT brought a new level of language understanding. Simultaneously, the Page Experience update made technical user experience a direct ranking factor. Google's Medic update introduced E-A-T as a critical framework.",
      "The focus intensified on content created for people, by people. The Helpful Content Update specifically targeted content designed to rank rather than help users. E-A-T became E-E-A-T with the addition of Experience. The March 2024 Core Update was a watershed moment that resulted in a 40% reduction in low-quality content.",
      "The content qualities Google spent 25 years learning to reward are the same qualities AI answer engines now look for.",
      "Search is undergoing its biggest transformation yet. AI Overviews appear directly in the SERP, synthesizing information from multiple sources. The challenge is to maintain visibility in a world of zero-click searches and to create content valuable enough to be cited by AI and clicked on by users. This is where SEO and Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) converge."
    ],
