    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "A curated timeline of major Google algorithm updates — with a Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) lens. Each entry explains what changed, who was affected, and what it means for your AI visibility strategy.",
      "Google's first update of 2026 — a core update focused specifically on the Discover feed, not general Search. Initially rolling out for English-language U.S. users before expanding to more countries and languages. Google also revised its Discover guidelines alongside this update.",
      "The third and final core update of 2025, launched December 11 and completed December 29. Affected search results globally. Early analysis showed more branded sites winning 'best of' and comparison queries, continuing Google's trend of favoring authoritative, first-party sources.",
      "A targeted spam update focused on search quality, rolling out from August 26 to September 21. This update refined Google's ability to detect and demote manipulative content patterns, including scaled content abuse and link manipulation schemes.",
      "The second core update of 2025, rolling out from June 30 to July 17. Google's John Mueller noted that core updates build on long-term data, not just recent changes. Analysis showed significant reshuffling in competitive niches, with content depth and user satisfaction signals playing a larger role.",
      "The first core update of 2025, rolling out from March 13 to March 27. Continued refinement of content quality signals, focused on improving how Google assesses content helpfulness and expertise, building on the foundation laid by the 2024 core updates.",
      "The final spam update of 2024, launched December 19 and completed December 26. A quick, targeted update that cleaned up remaining spam patterns identified during the year's core updates.",
      "A fast-rolling core update (only 6 days) that continued Google's push toward rewarding genuinely helpful content. This update refined the classifier introduced in earlier 2024 updates and adjusted how content quality is assessed at scale.",
      "A significant update rolling out alongside continued spam updates. Focused on better understanding content relationships and topical authority across entire sites rather than individual pages. Concluded on December 5.",
      "Focused on surfacing content created for people rather than search engines. Introduced refined signals for identifying content that provides genuine value versus content optimized purely for rankings."
    ],
