    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "Arize Phoenix is an open-source tool for LLM tracing, evaluation, and dataset curation that runs locally or in the cloud. This guide covers how to instrument chains, run evals against spans, and use the visual UI to debug retrieval and generation failures in RAG systems.",
      "Arize Phoenix is fully open-source (Apache 2.0) and runs locally — it's the only major LLM observability tool with no data leaving your infrastructure by default.",
      "Phoenix instruments at the span level: each retrieval call, LLM call, and tool use is a separate traceable span, giving you surgical visibility into multi-step chains.",
      "The built-in eval templates cover hallucination, relevance, toxicity, and Q&A correctness — all runnable as LLM-as-judge using any model you choose.",
      "Phoenix integrates with OpenTelemetry natively, meaning any OTel-compatible tracing already in your stack can feed Phoenix without additional instrumentation.",
      "Dataset curation from traces is Phoenix's unique strength: flag bad spans, export them as eval datasets, and close the loop from production failures to test coverage.",
      "Instrumentation: OpenTelemetry and auto-tracing",
      "Span-level tracing: surgical pipeline visibility",
      "The moment your organization's data governance team learns that every LLM trace is being sent to a third-party SaaS, the conversation about LLM observability changes. Arize Phoenix exists for exactly this scenario — and also for the broader category of teams that want open-source flexibility over a hosted product. It is the only major LLM observability tool that runs fully locally, with Apache 2.0 licensing, and OpenTelemetry-native instrumentation. Thi...",
      "Phoenix is an observability tool with evaluation capabilities. The distinction matters:"
    ],
