    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "Research benchmarks that evaluate GEO strategies across different engines and pipeline stages. Understand what works, what doesn't, and how to measure optimization effectiveness.",
      "1The Original GEO Paper: What Princeton & IIT Delhi Actually Found",
      "2CC-GSEO-Bench: The First Content-Centric Benchmark for Measuring Source Influence in Generative Search",
      "3AutoGEO (ICLR 2026): How CMU Built a Framework to Automatically Optimize Content for AI Visibility",
      "4C-SEO Bench (C-SEO Paper): Does Conversational SEO Actually Work?",
      "5SAGEO Arena: The First Realistic GEO Benchmark — Full Pipeline, 170K Documents, and Why Body-Text Optimization Fails",
      "AutoGEO automatically extracts what generative engines prefer and rewrites content to maximize visibility. Accepted at ICLR 2026, it introduces a cooperative approach — optimizing for GEO score (visibility) without destroying GEU score (utility). But SAGEO Arena found it degrades retrieval rank by −22.35.",
      "AutoGEO (CMU, ICLR 2026) automatically extracts what each generative engine prefers and rewrites content to match — no manual rule application needed.",
      "It introduces a cooperative tradeoff: GEO score (visibility) vs GEU score (utility) — improving visibility without destroying the model's answer quality.",
      "AutoGEOMini uses RL-based training to be roughly 10× cheaper than the API-based AutoGEOAPI version."
    ],
