    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "BrowseComp measures whether agents can persistently browse the web to find hard-to-locate facts. For GEO teams, that changes the job: your site is no longer just something to rank or cite, but something agents must successfully navigate, verify, and use.",
      "BrowseComp measures persistent web browsing with 1,266 hard problems — isolating the ability to navigate, cross-check, and verify fragmented evidence.",
      "Deep Research (o3) achieved the top score; standard language models scored below 2%, showing browsing capability is separate from language ability.",
      "The benchmark reveals a strategic GEO shift: optimize for agent navigation and verification, not just retrieval and citation.",
      "Your website is increasingly part of an agent's research workflow — not just a document in a search index.",
      "Practical implications: site navigation clarity, factual consistency across pages, and verifiable claims matter as much as content quality.",
      "What the results say about browsing agents",
      "The new job of SEO and GEO consultants",
      "A practical framework for agent-ready websites",
      "Most SEO and GEO conversations still assume the core problem is retrieval: can your page get found, ranked, and maybe cited? That assumption is becoming incomplete."
    ],
