      "Practical patterns for chunking strategy and metadata filters that keep retrieval on-topic.",
      "RAG fails because retrieval hands the model the wrong text — wrong context is the root bottleneck, not weak generation models.",
      "Chunking is a retrieval policy: chunks too large import irrelevant sentences; chunks too small strip the context the model needs.",
      "Semantic chunking (split at topic/section boundaries) outperforms fixed-size chunking for most document types.",
      "Metadata pre-filtering eliminates noise before vector scoring — tag chunks with document type, date, topic, and product area.",
      "Combined strategy: semantic chunking + metadata pre-filter → vector retrieval → reranker. Each layer handles what it's best at.",
      "RAG systems don’t fail because models are weak. They fail because retrieval hands the model the wrong text. This post breaks down how chunking and metadata filtering actually control retrieval precision, with practical patterns you can implement immediately.",
