      "3How to Make Your AI Content Trustworthy: DOI Verification",
      "A short cosine-dense summary can win retrieval, but a more useful document can win reranking.",
      "A short, cosine-dense summary won retrieval (embedding stage) but was outscored by a longer, evidence-rich document at the reranking stage.",
      "Retrieval is a gate (pass/fail on vector proximity); reranking is a judge (scored by evidence usefulness) — they optimize for different things.",
      "A cross-encoder reranker correctly demoted the generic summary because it scored relevance, not vector similarity.",
      "Optimizing only for cosine similarity can make content thinner and more generic — the opposite of what rerankers reward.",
      "Real-pipeline GEO requires satisfying both stages: retrievable enough to pass the gate AND useful enough to win the judge."
