    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "GA4's default channel group has no AI Search definition — and you can't edit it. Here's how to create a custom channel group that labels ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini, Claude, and Copilot traffic as a first-class channel in every report.",
      "GA4's Default Channel Group cannot be edited — you create a parallel custom channel group that adds 'AI Search' as a first-class channel alongside the existing defaults.",
      "Navigate to Admin → Data display → Channel groups → Create new channel group. Add a channel named 'AI Search' with Session source matching regex for all major AI engine domains.",
      "Place AI Search above Referral in the channel priority list — GA4 evaluates top-to-bottom and assigns the first matching definition, so AI Search must come before the catch-all Referral rule.",
      "Custom channel groups apply from the date of creation forward. GA4 does not reprocess historical sessions, so create yours now and allow 30 days before drawing trend conclusions.",
      "The custom group appears as a dimension option throughout GA4 — Traffic acquisition reports, Explorations, comparisons, and segments all support it once created.",
      "Why the default channel group doesn't work",
      "Step-by-step: create the custom channel group",
      "How to use the custom channel group in reports",
      "GA4 ships with a Default Channel Group that includes 29 channel definitions. None of them cover AI Search. The system default cannot be modified — but GA4 lets you create a parallel custom channel group that sits alongside the default and surfaces \"AI Search\" as a labeled channel across all reports."
    ],
