    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "DeepSeek V4 (released April 24, 2026) ships a 1-million-token context window using just 9.62 GB of KV cache — an 8.7× reduction over V3.2. Hybrid Attention combines 4:1 and 128:1 compression, sparse top-512 selection, and a 128-token sliding window. Here's the architecture, the benchmarks, and why GPT-5.5 and Claude Opus 4.7 now face 6× cost pressure.",
      "DeepSeek V4 (released 24 April 2026) ships 1-million-token context with just 9.62 GiB of KV cache per sequence — an 8.7× reduction versus a 61-layer V3.2-style stack at 83.9 GiB.",
      "Hybrid Attention combines four mechanisms: shared K/V vectors with inverse RoPE (2× saving), Compressed Sparse Attention at 4:1 ratio with top-512 selection (CSA), Heavily Compressed Attention at 128:1 with dense attention (HCA), and a 128-token sliding window for local fidelity.",
      "Real-world impact: 73% reduction in per-token FLOPs and sustained throughput >150 tokens/second/user at 1M context on NVIDIA GB200 NVL72 hardware.",
      "Pricing: V4-Pro processes 1M input tokens for ~$2 versus ~$12 on GPT-5.5 and Claude Opus 4.7 — a structural 6× cost advantage DeepSeek has declared permanent, not promotional.",
      "Benchmarks: V4-Pro beats GPT-5.4 on Codeforces (3,206 vs 3,168), hits 91.2% on SWE-Bench Verified (close behind Claude Opus 4.7's 93.9%), and a survey of 85 developers found 52% consider it ready to replace their primary coding model.",
      "Why Are 1-Million-Token Contexts Still a Memory Nightmare for Most Models?",
      "What Did DeepSeek V4 Actually Change Architecturally?",
      "How Does Compressed Sparse Attention (CSA) Compress the KV Cache 4×?",
      "What Does Heavily Compressed Attention (HCA) Do at a 128:1 Ratio?"
    ],
