    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "E-GEO benchmarks e-commerce Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) and shows why prompt optimization beats copywriting heuristics.",
      "E-GEO introduces a benchmark for e-commerce GEO — measuring how product description rewrites move ranking in LLM-generated recommendations.",
      "Traditional 'write better copy' heuristics (keywords, clarity, concision) produce only modest ranking gains in the benchmark.",
      "Treating GEO as an optimization problem — specifically optimizing the rewriting prompt itself — delivers significantly stronger results.",
      "E-GEO pipeline: retrieval pulls a candidate set, then an LLM re-ranks and explains recommendations — visibility = rank in the LLM's output.",
      "What makes a product description win in LLM recommendations is different from what wins in traditional keyword search.",
      "Generative engines (LLM-powered \"answer + recommendations\" systems) are quickly replacing the old \"10 blue links\" workflow—especially in commerce, where users ask multi-sentence, constraint-heavy questions and expect a ranked shortlist back. The original GEO paper from Princeton and IIT Delhi laid the groundwork; E-GEO extends it to e-commerce.",
      "The E-GEO paper introduces a benchmark for e-commerce Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) and shows that “write better copy” heuristics are weak until you treat Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) as an optimization problem.",
      "If you’re new to answer-first funnels, start with Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) vs SEO: How the User Funnel Has Changed for the high-level shift, then come back here for the benchmark details.",
      "Paper: E-GEO: A Testbed for Generative Engine Optimization in E-Commerce Authors: Puneet S. Bagga, Vivek F. Farias, Tamar Korkotashvili, Tianyi Peng, Yuhang Wu"
    ],
