    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "LangSmith is LangChain's observability and evaluation platform. This guide covers how to instrument any LLM application for tracing, build eval datasets from production runs, run automated evaluators, and use the annotation queue for human review.",
      "LangSmith works with any LLM framework (not just LangChain) — a single environment variable wraps any OpenAI or Anthropic call in full trace logging.",
      "The trace-to-dataset pipeline is LangSmith's killer feature: flag any production run, add it to a dataset, and use it as a regression test case in one click.",
      "LangSmith's evaluator library includes pre-built criteria evaluators (correctness, helpfulness, conciseness) plus custom code and LLM-based scorers.",
      "The annotation queue lets you route specific traces to human reviewers, creating labeled data that feeds both fine-tuning and eval dataset improvement.",
      "Online evaluation in LangSmith samples live production traffic and scores it automatically, giving you a continuous quality signal without manual spot-checking.",
      "The annotation queue: human review workflow",
      "Online evaluation: scoring production traffic",
      "LangSmith solves a problem that every team building with LLMs eventually hits: you can see that the application produced an answer, but you cannot see why. Which prompt was used? What context was retrieved? How many tokens did the chain consume? What did the intermediate steps produce? LangSmith answers all of these — and then lets you evaluate, annotate, and regression-test the results. This guide covers the setup, the core workflows, and when LangSmit...",
      "LangSmith has two distinct capabilities that are easy to conflate:"
    ],
