      "2Chain-of-Thought Prompting for Content",
      "Treat prompts as testable systems — build scoring rubrics, run A/B tests, catch regression, and iterate toward consistently excellent output.",
      "Prompts are probabilistic systems — the same prompt produces different outputs, and untested prompts have unknown variance.",
      "Build a scoring rubric (1–5 scale across 3–5 criteria) before A/B testing to prevent confirmation bias in evaluation.",
      "A/B testing prompts requires running each variant on the same 10–20 test cases for a meaningful comparison."
