    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "A practical guide to RAGAS metrics, workflows, and scoring pitfalls.",
      "RAGAS separates RAG failure modes: faithfulness (generation quality), context relevance (retrieval quality), and answer relevance (alignment to question).",
      "High faithfulness + low context relevance = model is correctly faithful to wrong context — this is a retriever problem, not a generator problem.",
      "Build evaluation datasets from real user queries with human-verified answers — synthetic datasets systematically overstate performance.",
      "Use RAGAS scores directionally to compare pipeline variants, not as absolute quality benchmarks.",
      "Running RAGAS before and after changes reveals which component is responsible for quality shifts.",
      "RAGAS is a practical evaluation toolkit for retrieval-augmented generation that helps engineers measure whether answers are grounded, relevant, and useful. This post breaks down what each metric captures and how to use it without fooling yourself.",
      "The core RAGAS metrics and what they really measure",
      "How to build an evaluation dataset that doesn’t lie",
      "Interpreting scores without cargo-culting them"
    ],
