    "paragraphHighlights": [
      "Hygiene is not SEO. Hygiene is table stakes. Here's the uncomfortable truth about what separates consultants who move the needle from those who just follow checklists.",
      "Hygiene-only SEO — canonical tags, crawlability, sitemap submissions — is already being automated. It is table stakes, not a value proposition.",
      "Google's revenue model runs on paid ads. Every organic result is Google competing against itself. Good consultants understand these conflicting incentives; bad ones treat Google as a partner.",
      "Every ranking signal Google measures is a proxy for one question: did the user get what they wanted and not come back for more?",
      "The job is not to follow rules — rules are the floor. The job is to find the one edge that makes your client the only logical answer to a query.",
      "The attitude divide: bad consultants ask 'are we following best practices?'; good consultants ask 'what can we do that nobody else is doing?'",
      "Is the \"hygiene only\" SEO already dead?",
      "What is the one reward function that drives every ranking?",
      "Is SEO a problem you ever actually finish?",
      "What separates the good consultants from the bad ones?"
    ],
